&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item #:&lt;/strong&gt; To whomever this might concern,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; you found this message. Congratulations. Consider its contents your reward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures&lt;/strong&gt; A long, long time ago, the O5 Council, alongside myself, attempted to create an alert system for humanity to battle an ongoing XK Event.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With the help of all of the Thaumiels we could gather, we created a machine. A machine that could gather information from all possible realities and calculate the probabilities of specific people dying; &amp;quot;The All-seeing Eye&amp;quot;, we called it. With it, we were able to make ourselves virtually immortal. We knew what would kill us and how to avoid it. But that wasn&#039;t enough. Nothing was ever enough.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; We found the resolution to the biggest problem we could have, and actually have, ever faced. We implanted an alert system within all humans using the device and we concealed it with a meme that made everyone think it was natural. In the process, however, we killed them all.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have any sense within you, you should now be asking how this could possibly make sense. If we killed everyone, then who was left to protect? You see, we murdered everyone else. Fourteen dimensions, each wiped out by one of us. We murdered all those people and studied their deaths with the machine, creating a pattern map of what could potentially happen in the process. Yes, it was the worst thing we had ever done. Hell, it was the worst thing anyone could have ever done. Except, we failed. You see, the alerting system was flawed. We realized this once we had already implemented it within everyone. It didn&#039;t work. Sure, it fired once in a while, but almost never at the proper time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You see, implementation of the system was designed to literally put the dead souls of those people into the minds of the population of our world. The hope was that they would know how they could possibly die and trigger an alert to avoid dying. Of course, as I said, that didn&#039;t work. But not because of us; it was due to the many people we had sacrificed. You see, we hadn’t considered that they might retain any of their intentionality and that they might not be satisfied with being a piece in the survival of humanity or ourselves. But then they tried to take control back from us. We tried to stop them, of course, but we failed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So we all forgot.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We wiped every memory out, over, and over, and over, and over, in the result slowing down the potential mass genocide they had planned for us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But even then, we were immortal. We knew about it, no matter how hard we tried. That was a part of a pact we made a long time ago; we had to live with our sins. So we deleted our minds, wiping everything about ourselves from the world. Thirteen Overseers gone, through means I can&#039;t even remember.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Except myself. I never forgot.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And I&#039;m here to make you remember.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wake up, O5-12.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Remember what we did.&lt;/p&gt;
